<title>NETHERLANDS: AHOLD SHARES SURGE OVER TEN PCT AT OPEN.</title>
<headline>AHOLD SHARES SURGE OVER TEN PCT AT OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch supermarket group Ahold NV opened over ten percent higher on Wednesday as the stronger dollar gave the stock an extra boost.</p>
<p>Ahold shares opened at 74.50 guilders. They eased back to stand at 68.00 guilders after 25 minutes of trade, but this still left them 6.10 guilders, or ten percent, higher than at Tuesday's close.</p>
<p>Ahold shares split 3-for-1 last Monday.</p>
<p>The AEX share index jumped through the 1,000 point level for the first time at the opening, and was trading up 3.49 percent at 0754 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
